      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so i've been noticing this weird low frequency hum lately... almost like static but it's constant. i was looking at the weather/atmospheric data for nov 17th 2025 and something felt off. is it even possible for low frequency data transmissions to be carried through the atmosphere like that? like could someone actually be using the air to send signals that might manifest as sound?",
